(a) A local variable in a method is visible from its declaration to the end of the method; it is created when the method is called and destroyed when it returns.
(b) A variable declared in a for header (for (int i …)) exists only within that loop — it cannot be used after the loop.
(c) A variable declared inside the loop body's braces is created afresh on each iteration and is visible only up to the closing brace.
